  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2025/1/IncidentResponseSecurityOntology#Playbook_p582">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2025/1/IncidentResponseSecurityOntology#Playbook"/>
    <irso:hasPlaybookID rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">p582</irso:hasPlaybookID>
    <irso:hasPlaybookName rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Orchestrate Automox Vulnerability Sync with Rapid7 InsightVM</irso:hasPlaybookName>
    <irso:hasPlaybookDescription rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"> Setup Import the workflow from the Rapid7 Extension Library and proceed through the Import Workflow wizard in InsightConnect. Import plugins, create or select connections, and rename the workflow as a part of the Import Workflow wizard as necessary. There are three workflow parameters you will need to configure in order to complete setup of your workflow:* `Automox Organization ID`: The identifier of the Automox organization.* `CVEs in Scope`: Comma separated list of CVEs in scope for immediate remediation between InsightVM and Automox.* `Auto-Approve Tasks`: Whether to auto-approve and apply patches for identified vulnerabilities immediately. </irso:hasPlaybookDescription>
    <irso:providedBy rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2025/1/IncidentResponseSecurityOntology#Vendor_Rapid7"/>
