  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2025/1/IncidentResponseSecurityOntology#Playbook_p1037">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2025/1/IncidentResponseSecurityOntology#Playbook"/>
    <irso:hasPlaybookID rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">p1037</irso:hasPlaybookID>
    <irso:hasPlaybookName rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Dedup - Generic v3</irso:hasPlaybookName>
    <irso:hasPlaybookDescription rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This playbook identifies duplicate incidents using one of the supported methods. Select one of the following methods to identify duplicate incidents in Cortex XSOAR. - ml: Machine learning model, which is trained mostly on phishing incidents. -rules: Rules help identify duplicate incidents when the logic is well defined, for example, the same label or custom fields. -text: Statistics algorithm that compares text, which is generally useful for phishing incidents. For each method, the playbook will search for the oldest similar incident. when there is a match for a similar incident the playbook will close the current incident and will link it to the older incident. </irso:hasPlaybookDescription>
    <irso:providedBy rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2025/1/IncidentResponseSecurityOntology#Vendor_XSOAR"/>
    <irso:hasStep rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/user/ontologies/2025/1/IncidentResponseSecurityOntology#Step_s13961"/>
